  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1020 PM MDT Sat Aug 1 2026\n\nUpper high stays over Arizona heading into Sunday. High pressure \nbroadens and flattens Monday through mid-week. What this means for \nus is a rebound in temperatures Monday through Wednesday where many \nlowland locations will see triple digit highs during this time. \nContinued monsoonal thunderstorms each afternoon with a primary \nfocus over the are mountains and western locations of the CWA \nnearing Arizona. By late in the work week, high pressure looks to \nmove over Nevada and away from us to give us *some* relief, but not \nmuch. Maybe a handful of degrees shaved off for Thursday and \nFriday compared to Wednesdays highs. Looks like better chances of \nrain will be possible for more of the area late in the week.",
